docs/proposals/owner-questions-review/codex.out:676:_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:524:Raw types are `*const T` / `*mut T` (slice 24). Dereference/store use unary `*` and place assignment; `as` is not a blanket pointer/integer conversion mechanism: reference-to-raw conversion is gated by [OD98](../docs/decisions.md#od98). Reference-to-reference casts are refused ([OD103](../docs/decisions.md#od103)); pointer/integer round trips use Q3.9’s `expose` / `from_exposed`, not an invented `as` conversion. Integers carry no pointer provenance; every raw access requires typed validity/provenance/aliasing premises (Core Q3.7–Q3.11). Reference-derived pointers stay confined to the borrow and can never reach a kept parameter; kept retention transfers an owned allocation H by value and returns a linear Kept<H> receipt ([OD64](../docs/decisions.md#od64), Core Q3.12). A write derived from shared &T remains forbidden ([OD112](../docs/decisions.md#od112)).
docs/proposals/owner-questions-review/codex.out:685:_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:647:21. **OPEN-21 — API/view spellings and branded signatures (7/15/16/19/21–27).** Recommend View/ViewMut second-class parameter constructors and ordinary calls for the decided ct_select/ct_eq/text/container APIs; use exact explicit branded type arguments; floating conversions use `name::<Target>(x)`. Alternative: &[]-style view types and qualified associated APIs. Reason: feature names in Q3/Q4 and the information-flow decision do not decide every arity, type position, qualifier or conversion target syntax. Submit the exhaustive concrete signature table before encoding it; no fabricated complete signatures here.
