docs/proposals/owner-questions-review/codex.out:757:docs/decisions.md:225:- **Q3.7** What is the raw-memory model and validity taxonomy? — Blocks with provenance; pointer = (prov: Option<BlockId>, addr: u64); integers carry no provenance; every access needs explicit validity premises. *Generalized 2026-11-08 by the [foundation decision](#foundation-q3): the address is read from a read-only target profile; the existing 64-bit little-endian profile is unchanged, and the provenance rules and the zero-byte exception are preserved.*
docs/proposals/owner-questions-review/codex.out:758:docs/decisions.md:227:- **Q3.9** What do pointer equality and integer round trips mean? — `expose` records the block; `from_exposed` picks in-bounds, then one-past, else no provenance. *Generalized 2026-11-08 by the [foundation decision](#foundation-q3): over the target profile's address spaces; the reconstruction policy is unchanged.*
